2. Where any instrument or object has been seized or removed under section 13L(7) of the Act, the community relations officer who seized or removed the instrument or object must —
(a)record the location, date and time at which the instrument or object was seized or removed;
(b)consolidate the record mentioned in paragraph (a) together with the records of all other instruments or objects (if any) seized or removed at the same location and date;
(c)cause a copy of the records mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) (as the case may be) to be given to the owner or occupier of the place of residence from which the instruments or objects were seized or removed; and
(d)cause the instrument or object seized or removed to be kept or stored at a place of safety or any other suitable place determined by the community relations officer.
